I've completed the review and written it to `_review.md`. Summary of findings:

**What the agent did:** Replaced the unreliable raw-ID dedup with a normalized-link identity (stripping `utm_*` params) and added a per-channel `deliveries` ledger, so items are only sent once per channel. I verified this empirically — re-running the same fixture snapshot produces zero duplicate sends, and transitioning from snapshot-a to snapshot-b correctly delivers only the genuinely new item while suppressing the rotated-campaign, regenerated-guid, and edited-content cases.

